C-P2-1_fix: src/cli/forge.ts checks the view names of render, all, animate, inspect, and cutout before the server starts and before the build. viewNamesOf(command, values) gives each command its own list (the --views list or the command default); checkViewNames refuses an unknown name with one line through the top-level error handler, so the exit code is 1, the output is one line, and no stack frame prints. Raw output: "Unknown view 'nosuch'. Known: front, three-quarter, side, back, back-three-quarter, top, front-level, side-level". The output folder did not appear (GATE_D_UNKNOWN_VIEW_OUT_DIR_EXISTS=no), because the build never runs.
B-F1_fix: src/pipeline.ts exports checkAssetName(name); assetPath calls it before it builds a path. An empty, absolute, separator, or dot-dot name is refused with one line and a non-zero exit. The CLI checks the worn piece names too, before the output name is built. Raw output of the traversal: "Invalid asset name '../measure/runs/chibi_sprouts_redesign_20261123/probe-escape-green': an asset name has no path separator." Raw output of the separator: "Invalid asset name 'a/b': an asset name has no path separator." The traversal wrote nothing outside out/ (GATE_D_TRAVERSAL_LEAK=no). A name with a dot or a dash and the _flat-render-pin-<pid> fixture name still work.
B-F1_fix_flat_removal: removeFlatFolder(flatDir, outRoot) in src/cli/forge.ts replaces the recursive delete of the flat folder. It removes nothing when the folder is a symlink, and it removes the folder only when the real path of its parent sits directly under the real out/ root. A symlinked output folder is never followed and never deleted. The flat folder is removed only after the asset name check passed.
